    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a high-upside matchup against Sugano today, fueling **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (69.94) to lead the offensive charge. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as our premier start; his elite 81.88 score is bolstered by a significant SP skill advantage (+19%) and park factors that play perfectly into his profile. While **Luis Robert Jr.** faces a minor platoon headwind, the favorable matchup against Sugano makes him a high-floor start. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (73.26) remains a set-and-forget cornerstone, benefiting from a positive SP skill discrepancy (+7%) and a prime spot in the heart of the order.\n\nTactical adjustments highlight our push for efficiency, specifically regarding **Kyle Tucker** (50.23). While his talent level is immense, the matchup against a formidable arm in Mautz (xERA 2.71) suppresses his ceiling, narrowly keeping him above our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold. On the bench, **Wade Meckler** (37.29) and **Liam Hicks** (36.92) were the most difficult exclusions. Despite **Wade Meckler** enjoying favorable platoon splits, the combination of a tough opposing arm in Schlittler and our stringent 40-point efficiency floor forced his benching to preserve our limited game caps for more optimal matchups. We are closely monitoring **Heliot Ramos** (48.17); while he provides a slight boost in the stolen base department\u2014a critical focus for the Waves\u2014his performance against Detmers carries inherent risk due to the pitcher's efficiency, making him a marginal play today.",
